On Aug 20, 9:18 am, MJneth...@gmail.com wrote:
> I've read several times that one should fight big baddies from the
> upstair, so they can't escape upstairs or heal up away from you.  I've
> had trouble putting this into practice, though.
>
> 1: How do you get onto the upstair without chasing him upstairs
> first?  Asmodeus' lair, at least, is no-teleport.

Covetous monsters (such as Asmodeus and arch-liches) will also follow
you downstairs or through a hole in the ground.  Just go down to a
level where you _can_ teleport to the upstairs.  Wait for them to move
to you to attack and then self-teleport or jump onto the upstairs.
>
> 2. Once with an arch-lich or maybe Juiblex I ported to the upstair,
> but he just stayed away.  I had to go chase him, and then he ported to
> the stair and escaped.

That's unusual; but perhaps you were on a level with 2 upstairs and
you were originally on the wrong one.  Also, I think that sometimes
they will stay away if wounded but usually they will hop around you
while they get whacked to death.



